  "title": "Karl A NDE 6946",
  "date": "ca. 1968",
  "content": "I fell down from a carriage under a wheel. The wheel dragged me, but didn't run over me. I left my body and was floating above myself. In the distance, I saw an indescribable bright light. I saw myself lying under the wheel. I was swinging back and forth between the light and myself. I saw my father as he struggled to take care of me. As long as I was outside myself, I didn't feel pain: only calm and peace. Suddenly, I was back again. I felt strong pain. I had bad crushes and a broken upper arm. In this condition I was delivered to the hospital.",
